            <ArticleTitle>[A preliminary study of pentanucleotide repeat polymorphism of apolipoprotein(a) gene in coronary atherosclerotic heart disease].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">This study inquired into the relationship between a pentanucleotide repeats(PNR) polymorphism of the apolipoprotein(a)[apo(a)] gene and coronary atherosclerotic heart disease(CHD) in Chinese Han nationality.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">PNR polymorphism of the apo(a) gene from 165 cases of CHD and 153 normal individuals were analyzed by polymerase chain reaction(PCR)-denature polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis-silver stain.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The frequencies of (TTTTA)(5/8) genotype (0.188) and (TTTTA)(5) allele (0.115) in CHD group were remarkably higher than those in control group (0.039, 0.026)(P&lt;0.01, P&lt;0.05).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">These findings indicate that the PNR polymorphism of apo(a) is associated with the susceptibility to CHD, which may be involved in the development of CHD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
